<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
	<head>
		<%-include("../partials/header.ejs")%>
	</head>
	<body>
		<%-include("../partials/menu.ejs")%>
		<section class="main">
			<div class="scrollable">
				<h1>About</h1>

				<p>Blairpath is a web app supplying maps and route calculation for the campus of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_Blair_High_School">Montgomery Blair High School (MBHS)</a>.</p>

				<div class="banner gray">
					<p><b>Disclaimer:</b> Every few years, the MBHS campus adds or removes some portables, which must be manually registered by a Blairpath developer. Some parts of the map might be outdated.</p>
				</div>

				<section style="display: table; width: 100%">
					<div class="left">
						<h3>Team</h3>
						<p><a href="https://jeffreytong.me/"><b>Jeffrey Tong</b></a> (MBHS Class of 2022) founded and developed Blairpath (and maintains and funds it).</p>
					</div>
					<div class="right">
						<h3>Statistics</h3>
						<ul>
							<li><b><%-verticesArray.filter(v => v.section != "border" && v.section != "path").length%></b> places</li>
							<li><b><%-new Set(verticesArray.map(v => v.fxy.split(',')[0])).size%></b> floors</li>
							<li><b><%-verticesArray.length%></b> vertices</li>
							<li><b><%-diskData.edges.length%></b> edges</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</section>

				<h3>History</h3>
				<p><b>1998</b>: The present-day MBHS campus was completed. The architect wrote a <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20200222231349/http://www.designshare.com/HighSchoolLibrary/HSBlair/Blair2_Prog.htm">program summary</a>. They also shared their floor plans, which Blairpath's maps are based on (<a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20120205151339im_/http://www.designshare.com/HighSchoolLibrary/HSBlair/BlairSite.jpg">Site</a>, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160505145914im_/http://www.designshare.com/HighSchoolLibrary/HSBlair/blairpl1.jpg">Floor 1</a>, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160505225805im_/http://www.designshare.com/HighSchoolLibrary/HSBlair/blairpl2.gif">Floor 2</a>, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20120205151407im_/http://www.designshare.com/HighSchoolLibrary/HSBlair/blairpl3.gif">Floor 3</a>).</p>
				<p><b>2019</b>: Jeffrey developed a Blairpath prototype as a project for a MBHS computer science class, with most of the branding inspired by <a href="https://github.com/blairsec/blairbash">Blairbash.org</a> (now <a href="https://blairbash.ai/">Blairbash.ai</a>).
				<p><b>2021</b>: Jeffrey started renting the domain <code>blairpath.org</code>. MBHS teacher Mr. Schwartz showed Blairpath to his 9th grade students to introduce them to campus.</p>

				<h3>Contributing</h3>
				<p>To learn how to edit the map, read the <a href="https://github.com/spiralsim/blairpath/wiki/Blairpath-Dev-Tools-Tutorial">Blairpath Dev Tools Tutorial</a>.</p>
				<p>Blairpath is <a href="https://github.com/spiralsim/blairpath">open-source on GitHub</a> and welcomes Issues and Pull Requests.</p>

				<h3>Finances</h3>
				<p>Blairpath costs $77/year to operate ($17/year for the domain, $5/month for the application container).</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</body>
</html>